      "answer": "Based on my investigation, I found the answer to your question about the quaystone library's retry ceiling change:\n\nThe change occurred in version 4.2.0 of the quaystone library. \n\nWhat changed: The retry ceiling now counts attempts rather than retries. This means that if a configuration previously specified a value of 6, it would now mean 7 attempts (since the count includes the initial attempt plus the retries). In other words, the counting logic was modified to include the original attempt in the total count, rather than just counting the additional retry attempts.\n\nThis is documented in the changelog which shows that version 4.2.0 specifically mentions \"The retry ceiling now counts attempts rather than retries. A config that said 6 before means 7 now.\"",
